  "description": "VAWKAI crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 2 m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H108 Co4 Dy4 N4 O32,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.333-3.833 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.69-119.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoIII4DyIII4(μ-OH)4(μ3-OMe)4{O2CC(CH3)3}4(tea)4(H2O)4]·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 tea (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(II).",
